{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017UMiksr6qW9ap8mLdy2iwd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# TODO — Implement SOS cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257\n2\t\n3\tThis is a prepared execution plan. It tells you **what to build first**, gives\n4\t**rough guidance on how** (which existing engine seam to reuse, which FDN card\n5\tto mirror), and lists the **pitfalls** to avoid. It is a *guide, not a spec* —\n6\t`card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt` are the source of truth. When the real engine\n7\tdisagrees with a claim here, trust the engine and the spec, fix the code, and jot\n8\ta one-line note next to the item. See `CONTEXT.md` for the vocabulary used below.\n9\t\n10\tYou are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and\n11\tmechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make\n12\tchanges that don't break current behavior.\n13\t\n14\t## Prime directive\n15\t\n16\tOne mind builds all ten cards. The goal is **surgical, additive reuse**: build\n17\tor learn each shared seam once, then reuse it. The trap on cards like these is\n18\tbuilding a **separate general engine subsystem for each single-card mechanic** —\n19\tdo that six times and you get sprawling, speculative machinery where a handful of\n20\tsmall, focused edits would do, and that machinery tends to drift from what the\n21\tcards actually do. Keep changes small and local. Read `## Pitfalls` before you\n22\twrite any engine code.\n23\t\n24\t## The engine already supports most of this — reuse, don't rebuild\n25\t\n26\tRead the source for exact signatures and docstrings; do **not** trust any spec\n27\tdoc over the actual `engine/*.py`. These shared seams already exist and cover the\n28\tbulk of the ten cards:\n29\t\n30\t| Capability | Existing seam (read the source) | Mirror this FDN card | Reused by |\n31\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n32\t| Cost reduction (generic only) | `CardImpl.cost_reduction(self, game)` hook in `engine/card.py`; called by `get_cost_reduction` in `engine/casting.py` | fdn_57 | sos_1, sos_245 |\n33\t| Cast without paying, from any zone | `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` in `engine/casting.py` | fdn_194 (Etali), fdn_161 (Omniscience) | sos_1 (graveyard), sos_13 + sos_120 (exile) |\n34\t| Copy a spell on the stack | `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` in `engine/stack.py` (resolves via `on_resolve`, fires no cast event — copies are not \"cast\") | fdn_248 | sos_120, sos_226 |\n35\t| Colors / amount of mana spent | `card.colors_spent` set at cast time in `engine/casting.py` (~line 229); deterministic in tests via `mana_pool.pay(cost, choices=...)` | — | sos_4 (colors), sos_57 (amount) |\n36\t| Triggered abilities | `register_triggers(self, game)` hook + `TriggerRegistration` / `game.trigger_manager.register(...)` in `engine/triggers.py`; event classes in `engine/events.py` | fdn_235, fdn_81 | most cards |\n37\t| Replacement effects (zone redirect) | `register_replacement_effects(self, game)` hook + `ReplacementEffect`; set `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"` | fdn_244, fdn_137 | sos_1 (\"exile instead\") |\n38\t| Loyalty abilities | `Planeswalker` + `get_loyalty_abilities()` → `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; read targets from `self.chosen_targets` (the engine sets it from the activation's targets; mirror fdn_81 only for the loyalty scaffolding, not its `_resolve_target` reads) | fdn_44, fdn_81 | sos_97 |\n39\t| Mana abilities | `Land` + `get_mana_abilities()` → `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` | (grep fdn lands) | sos_257 |\n40\t| Counter target spell | card-local: mirror an FDN counterspell's local `_counter_spell` (pop from stack → graveyard) + `can_cast` guard + `zone=Zone.STACK` targeting | fdn_48 (Refute) | sos_57 |\n41\t| Tokens | `create_token(game, player, token)` in `engine/game.py` | fdn_44, fdn_81 | sos_13 |\n42\t| Reanimate (graveyard → battlefield) | `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB automatically) | — | sos_97 (−2) |\n43\t| Helpers | `engine/game.py`: `draw_card`, `discard`, `deal_damage`, `exile`, `sacrifice`, `add_counter`, `tap`/`untap` | — | many |\n44\t\n45\tBefore adding anything to `engine/`, confirm the seam above doesn't already do\n46\tthe job. The first question for every clause is **\"which FDN card and which\n47\texisting hook already does this?\"** — not \"what new system do I need?\".\n48\t\n49\t## Build these three shared engine changes FIRST (small, additive)\n50\t\n51\tEach is reused by more than one card. Build and verify them up front so the cards\n52\tthat depend on them just register ordinary triggers/hooks. Keep each tiny; run\n53\t`python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each.\n54\t\n55\t- **E1 — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`.** It is defined in `engine/events.py`\n56\t  (fields: `spell`, `card`, `controller`) but **never fired**. Fire it inside\n57\t  `cast_spell` (`engine/casting.py`) right after the spell is pushed to the stack,\n58\t  populating `spell=<the StackObject>`, `card`, and `controller`. Copies made by\n59\t  `copy_spell` do **not** go through `cast_spell`, so they correctly do not\n60\t  re-fire it. *Reused by:* sos_226 (Casualty), sos_257 (animated pump).\n61\t- **E2 — Add `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`.** No event fires at any\n62\t  main phase today. Add the event class to `engine/events.py` (model it on the\n63\t  fieldless `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`) and fire it from\n64\t  `GameState.advance_phase` (`engine/game_state.py`) — the single chokepoint every\n65\t  phase transition passes through — when the new phase becomes `PRECOMBAT_MAIN`,\n66\t  right **after** `empty_mana_pools()` so anything a handler adds to the pool\n67\t  survives into the main phase. Firing it here (not in `engine/turn.py`) makes it\n68\t  behave identically whether a turn is run normally or the state is advanced\n69\t  directly; a handler fired only from the turn loop would be skipped on a direct\n70\t  advance. Handlers identify \"your main phase\" by checking the active player.\n71\t  (Contrast E1, which belongs in `cast_spell` because casting always flows through\n72\t  that path.) *Reused by:* sos_57 (next main phase, once), sos_120 (each of your\n73\t  first main phases, recurring).\n74\t- **E3 — Aggregate cost reduction from the battlefield.** `get_cost_reduction`\n75\t  (`engine/casting.py`) only calls the spell's own `cost_reduction` hook. Extend\n76\t  it to also add reductions contributed by the caster's battlefield permanents:\n77\t  for each permanent exposing `spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell) -> int`,\n78\t  add it when the spell being cast is an instant/sorcery. Clamp as today\n79\t  (generic-only, ≥ 0). *Reused by:* sos_245 (grants affinity to your spells); any\n80\t  future \"your spells cost less\" card. (sos_1 / sos_245 self-reduction still use\n81\t  the normal `cost_reduction` hook.)\n82\t\n83\t## Per-card gaps — keep them CARD-LOCAL\n84\t\n85\tThe remaining mechanics each serve **exactly one card**. Implement each as the\n86\tsmallest local change in that card's `card_impl.py` (plus the tiny additive\n87\tengine edit noted), and add a one-line comment on any deliberate limitation. Do\n88\t**not** generalize these into engine subsystems. Specifics live in the per-card\n89\titems below: Miracle (sos_201), the split/back-face (sos_13), the restricted-mana\n90\ttag + land animation (sos_257), and coin-flips / skip-turns / surveil (sos_97).\n91\t\n92\t**E1–E3 and the per-card edits below are not an exhaustive list of the engine\n93\tchanges you may make.** If a card genuinely needs an engine change that isn't\n94\tlisted — a new event, a field on a permanent or on game state, a small helper —\n95\tyou are free to add it. The bar is *minimal, additive, and justified by a real\n96\tcard need*, not a fixed whitelist; what to avoid is a speculative general\n97\t*subsystem* for one card's mechanic, not engine edits as such. Whenever you touch\n98\t`engine/`, keep the change as small as possible, comment any deliberate\n99\tlimitation, never rename/move/delete existing symbols, and keep `engine_tests/`\n100\tgreen.\n101\t\n102\t## Build order\n103\t\n104\tWork the items **in order, one at a time**. Items E1–E3 are the shared engine\n105\tchanges above; the card items follow in dependency order (shared seams first,\n106\tthen the cards that reuse them; simplest → hardest). For every card: read its\n107\t`card_spec.json`, enumerate each oracle clause and its edges, mirror the nearest\n108\tFDN card, reuse the named seam, write 2–5 real-engine tests through `test_utils`,\n109\tthen run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` before moving on.\n110\t\n111\t- [ ] **E1 — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell`** (see above). Verify\n112\t  with a probe trigger that casting an instant fires it once with the right\n113\t  `controller` and `spell`.\n114\t- [ ] **E2 — Add + fire `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`** from\n115\t  `GameState.advance_phase`, after `empty_mana_pools()` (see above). Verify a\n116\t  registered trigger fires — and any mana it adds persists — when the state is\n117\t  advanced directly to the active player's precombat main.\n118\t- [ ] **E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction aggregation in `get_cost_reduction`**\n119\t  (see above). Verify a permanent exposing `spell_cost_reduction` reduces an\n120\t  instant's generic cost, clamped at 0.\n121\t\n122\t- [ ] **sos_4 — Together as One** *(warm-up: mana-spent, pure resolve)*\n123\t  - Clauses: Converge — X = number of colors of mana spent; target player draws\n124\t    X, deal X damage to any target, you gain X life.\n125\t  - Reuse: read `card.colors_spent` in `on_resolve`; `X = len(set(colors_spent))`.\n126\t    `draw_card`, `deal_damage`; set life directly. Targets via\n127\t    `get_targets`/`self.chosen_targets`.\n128\t  - Edges: X = 0 (colorless cast) → draws/deals/gains 0; \"any target\" is a player\n129\t    or creature. Tests set colors deterministically via `mana_pool.pay(choices=)`.\n130\t\n131\t- [ ] **sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic** *(cost reduction + free cast + trigger + replacement)*\n132\t  - Clauses: costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard; Reach; on\n133\t    attack, may cast target instant/sorcery from graveyard for free (if only one\n134\t    legal target, auto-select it instead of prompting); if that spell would go to\n135\t    the graveyard, exile it instead.\n136\t  - Reuse: `cost_reduction` hook (count instant/sorcery in your graveyard);\n137\t    `Keyword` for Reach; `register_triggers` on `AttacksTriggeredEvent`;\n138\t    `cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`; for exile-instead,\n139\t    register a `ReplacementEffect` that sets the spell's\n140\t    `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"`.\n141\t  - Edges: empty graveyard (no reduction; \"may\" trigger with no legal target);\n142\t    reduction is generic-only and clamps at 0.\n143\t\n144\t- [ ] **sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer** *(uses E3; affinity self + grant)*\n145\t  - Clauses: Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control);\n146\t    Flying, Deathtouch; your instant/sorcery spells also have affinity for creatures.\n147\t  - Reuse: `cost_reduction` hook for its OWN affinity (count creatures you\n148\t    control); `Keyword.FLYING | DEATHTOUCH`. For the grant, expose\n149\t    `spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)` returning your creature count — E3\n150\t    aggregates it into other spells' costs. No per-spell edits.\n151\t  - Edges: 0 creatures (no reduction); generic-only.\n152\t\n153\t- [ ] **sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant** *(uses E1; spell copy + casualty)*\n154\t  - Clauses: Flying, Vigilance; your instant/sorcery spells have Casualty 1.\n155\t  - Reuse: `register_triggers` on `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (now fired by E1),\n156\t    gated to instant/sorcery spells you cast while Silverquill is on the\n157\t    battlefield. On trigger, prompt once for the creature to sacrifice (one\n158\t    `choose_card`; the answer is the creature, or `None` to decline — no separate\n159\t    yes/no), and accept it only if its power ≥ 1 (`sacrifice`); if a creature is\n160\t    sacrificed, `copy_spell(game, event.spell, controller)` (the copy goes on the\n161\t    stack above the original and may choose new targets).\n162\t  - Edges: no creature with power ≥ 1 → casualty simply not taken; the copy is\n163\t    not itself \"cast\" (E1 won't re-fire for it — correct).\n164\t\n165\t- [ ] **sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex** *(uses E1; land: mana + restriction + animation)*\n166\t  - Clauses: {T}: add {C}; {T}, pay 1 life: add one mana of any color usable only\n167\t    to cast an instant/sorcery; {5}: if not already a creature, becomes a 2/4\n168\t    Wizard (still a land) with \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery, +1/+0 until EOT\".\n169\t  - Reuse: `Land` + `get_mana_abilities()` for the two mana abilities. The `{5}`\n170\t    animation is an **activated** ability — expose it via\n171\t    `get_activated_abilities(self)` (the engine calls this hook with no arguments\n172\t    and addresses abilities by printed index; do not add parameters to it). Read\n173\t    any state it needs from `self` — gate the animation on\n174\t    `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types` — not from a hook argument.\n175\t    `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (E1) drives the animated pump.\n176\t    **Restricted mana (gap):** add a lightweight restriction marker\n177\t    to mana in the pool and honor it at payment time so that mana can only pay for\n178\t    instant/sorcery spells (small additive change in `engine/mana.py`).\n179\t    **Animation (gap):** mutate in place — add the Creature type, base P/T 2/4, the\n180\t    Wizard subtype, and register the pump trigger; it stays a land. Do not make a\n181\t    new permanent.\n182\t  - Edges: animate only if not already a creature; the land has been on the\n183\t    battlefield, so no summoning sickness concern for the {5} clause; pump stacks\n184\t    per spell and resets end of turn; restricted mana cannot pay for a creature.\n185\t\n186\t- [ ] **sos_57 — Mana Sculpt** *(counter via fdn_48; uses E2)*\n187\t  - Clauses: counter target spell; if you control a Wizard, at the beginning of\n188\t    your next main phase add {C} equal to the mana spent to cast that spell.\n189\t  - Reuse: mirror **fdn_48 (Refute)** for the counter (local `_counter_spell`,\n190\t    `can_cast` guard, `zone=Zone.STACK` target). Record the countered spell's\n191\t    mana **spent** (amount, not mana value). Delayed mana: register a trigger on\n192\t    `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` (E2) stamped with the cast turn;\n193\t    when it next fires for you, if you control a Wizard add that much {C}, then\n194\t    unregister (one-shot).\n195\t  - Edges: no Wizard → no delayed mana; \"mana spent\" is the amount actually paid.\n196\t\n197\t- [ ] **sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone** *(cast-from-exile + copy; uses E2 for Paradigm)*\n198\t  - Clauses: exile from top of library until total mana value ≥ 4; may cast any\n199\t    number of them for free; Paradigm (after it first resolves, exile it; then at\n200\t    the beginning of each of your first main phases, may cast a copy from exile\n201\t    for free).\n202\t  - Reuse: library top access to peel cards (`library.top(n)`; top = last index);\n203\t    `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`; `copy_spell` for the Paradigm copy.\n204\t    Paradigm: on resolve exile the Capstone, then register a recurring trigger on\n205\t    `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` (E2) for your first main phase.\n206\t  - Edges: library runs out before MV 4; non-castable exiled cards (lands) stay\n207\t    exiled; \"first main phase\" = precombat main, recurring.\n208\t\n209\t- [ ] **sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares** *(uses cast-from-exile; token + prepared)*\n210\t  - Clauses: ETB — target player creates a 1/1 white-black Inkling with flying;\n211\t    then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes prepared;\n212\t    while prepared you may cast a copy of its spell (Swords to Plowshares),\n213\t    which unprepares it.\n214\t  - Reuse: one Creature class `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares` (3/3 Cat Cleric).\n215\t    **Bake its identity in so the class constructs bare** — set `name` to the full\n216\t    card name from `card_spec.json`, exactly `\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to\n217\t    Plowshares\"` (a double-faced card's name is the whole `front // back` string,\n218\t    not just the front face). The engine and tests instantiate the card with no\n219\t    arguments and key off `name`, so a front-face-only name makes it unfindable.\n220\t    Add a `SwordsToPlowshares(Instant)` **helper class in the same file** (exile\n221\t    target creature; its controller gains life = its power). `register_triggers`\n222\t    on `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`; `create_token`. When prepared and the\n223\t    player elects: create an **actual copy** of the Swords instant, put it in\n224\t    exile, and **cast it from exile** via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`, then\n225\t    unprepare. (Per the rulebook the prepared spell is a real Swords copy castable\n226\t    from exile — confirm cost semantics in `RULEBOOK.txt`.)\n227\t  - Edges: opponent does NOT control more creatures → not prepared; Swords on an\n228\t    empty board (no legal target).\n229\t\n230\t- [ ] **sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian** *(miracle card-local via draw event; upkeep loot)*\n231\t  - Clauses: Flying, Haste; instant/sorcery cards in your hand have miracle {2};\n232\t    at the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card to draw one.\n233\t  - Reuse: `Keyword.FLYING | HASTE`; `register_triggers` on\n234\t    `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` gated to an opponent's upkeep; `discard` +\n235\t    `draw_card`. **Miracle (gap, card-local):** register on\n236\t    `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` (already fired by `draw_card`), gated to your\n237\t    **first draw this turn** (track with a turn-stamped flag) AND drawn card is\n238\t    instant/sorcery; then you may cast it for the miracle cost by deducting {2}\n239\t    and using the free-cast stack path. Continuous effects do not reach the hand,\n240\t    so do not try to tag hand cards.\n241\t  - Edges: not the first card drawn this turn → no miracle; loot is optional;\n242\t    empty hand.\n243\t\n244\t- [ ] **sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer** *(planeswalker; surveil / reanimate / coin-flip / skip-turns)*\n245\t  - Clauses: starting loyalty 3; +1 Surveil 2; −1 any number of target players\n246\t    each discard a card; −2 return a creature card with mana value ≤ 3 from your\n247\t    graveyard to the battlefield; −7 flip five coins, target opponent skips their\n248\t    next X turns (X = heads).\n249\t  - Reuse: `Planeswalker` + `get_loyalty_abilities()` (mirror **fdn_81 / fdn_44**\n250\t    for the loyalty-ability scaffolding, but read this card's targets from\n251\t    `self.chosen_targets`, which the engine sets from the activation's `targets`\n252\t    — do not use `_resolve_target` / `_resolve_targets`). −2 reanimate via\n253\t    `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB). +1\n254\t    Surveil 2: look at `library.top(2)`, bin to graveyard or keep on top (small\n255\t    local helper; player choice in tests). **Coin flip (gap):** flip each coin\n256\t    with `random.Random.randint(0, 1)` via a seeded RNG — add a `game.rng`\n257\t    (`random.Random`) if absent so tests are deterministic. **Skip turns\n258\t    (gap):** record the count as a `skip_turns` attribute on the targeted player\n259\t    (`target_player.skip_turns += X`), and have the turn loop\n260\t    (`engine/game_state.py` advance logic) check and decrement it; X heads → skip\n261\t    that player's next X turns.\n262\t  - Edges: −2 with no valid creature in graveyard; −1 with zero target players;\n263\t    ultimate only at loyalty ≥ 7; X = 0 heads skips nothing.\n264\t\n265\t## Pitfalls (read before writing engine code)\n266\t\n267\t1. **A new subsystem for a one-card mechanic is the trap.** It is tempting to\n268\t   build generic miracle/casualty/affinity/paradigm/animation/preparation systems\n269\t   — but each here serves exactly one card, and that path balloons into sprawling,\n270\t   speculative machinery that drifts from the cards' real behavior. E1–E3 are the\n271\t   *shared* engine changes worth building up front (each reused by ≥ 2 cards);\n272\t   beyond them, add small additive engine edits whenever a single card genuinely\n273\t   needs one — just never a general *subsystem* for a one-card mechanic. If you're\n274\t   adding a manager, framework, or registry for something only one card uses, stop\n275\t   and make it card-local instead.\n276\t2. **Your own green tests are not proof.** Tests you write can encode the same\n277\t   misreading as your code — passing them only proves the code matches your\n278\t   reading, not the card. After each card, re-derive the behavior from\n279\t   `card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt` and run a short **throwaway** smoke check\n280\t   through `test_utils` that you did *not* write a test for — assert the\n281\t   spec-observable result (zones, life, P/T, counters, exile vs graveyard).\n282\t3. **Test through the real engine, never a stand-in.** Drive behavior via\n283\t   `test_utils` (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, `cast_spell`, `advance_to_phase`,\n284\t   `declare_attackers`, `declare_blockers`; for abilities, `ActivateAbility(card, index)`\n285\t   resolved through `priority_loop` and scripted with `DeterministicPlayer`).\n286\t   Abilities are addressed by printed index, the same way the engine activates them.\n287\t   Do not hand-build internal events, call a card's `get_*_abilities()` or\n288\t   `on_resolve` directly, pop the stack, or script a player's internal queue —\n289\t   those pass while the real path is broken.\n290\t4. **Reuse before you add.** For every clause, name the FDN card and existing hook\n291\t   that already does it before writing anything new. The seam table is the\n292\t   starting point; the FDN library is the rest.\n293\t5. **Additive-only, and keep `engine_tests/` green.** Add/extend in `engine/`; never\n294\t   rename/move/delete existing symbols — other modules import them by name, so a\n295\t   rename or move breaks those imports. Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q`\n296\t   after every card and every engine change; never ship a regression.\n297\t6. **Stay in the assigned file.** Each card's class lives in its own\n298\t   `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`; do not move or rename card directories. Do not\n299\t   edit `engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/*/tests.py`.\n300\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25473cdc-0503-4b45-9076-b9d3fca79f4a","uuid":"4671a55e-8fe3-41ca-b8db-70cccc7b0d4d","timestamp":"2026-06-10T16:34:11.507Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/TODO.md","content":"# TODO — Implement SOS cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257\n\nThis is a prepared execution plan. It tells you **what to build first**, gives\n**rough guidance on how** (which existing engine seam to reuse, which FDN card\nto mirror), and lists the **pitfalls** to avoid. It is a *guide, not a spec* —\n`card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt` are the source of truth. When the real engine\ndisagrees with a claim here, trust the engine and the spec, fix the code, and jot\na one-line note next to the item. See `CONTEXT.md` for the vocabulary used below.\n\nYou are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and\nmechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make\nchanges that don't break current behavior.\n\n## Prime directive\n\nOne mind builds all ten cards. The goal is **surgical, additive reuse**: build\nor learn each shared seam once, then reuse it. The trap on cards like these is\nbuilding a **separate general engine subsystem for each single-card mechanic** —\ndo that six times and you get sprawling, speculative machinery where a handful of\nsmall, focused edits would do, and that machinery tends to drift from what the\ncards actually do. Keep changes small and local. Read `## Pitfalls` before you\nwrite any engine code.\n\n## The engine already supports most of this — reuse, don't rebuild\n\nRead the source for exact signatures and docstrings; do **not** trust any spec\ndoc over the actual `engine/*.py`. These shared seams already exist and cover the\nbulk of the ten cards:\n\n| Capability | Existing seam (read the source) | Mirror this FDN card | Reused by |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cost reduction (generic only) | `CardImpl.cost_reduction(self, game)` hook in `engine/card.py`; called by `get_cost_reduction` in `engine/casting.py` | fdn_57 | sos_1, sos_245 |\n| Cast without paying, from any zone | `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` in `engine/casting.py` | fdn_194 (Etali), fdn_161 (Omniscience) | sos_1 (graveyard), sos_13 + sos_120 (exile) |\n| Copy a spell on the stack | `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` in `engine/stack.py` (resolves via `on_resolve`, fires no cast event — copies are not \"cast\") | fdn_248 | sos_120, sos_226 |\n| Colors / amount of mana spent | `card.colors_spent` set at cast time in `engine/casting.py` (~line 229); deterministic in tests via `mana_pool.pay(cost, choices=...)` | — | sos_4 (colors), sos_57 (amount) |\n| Triggered abilities | `register_triggers(self, game)` hook + `TriggerRegistration` / `game.trigger_manager.register(...)` in `engine/triggers.py`; event classes in `engine/events.py` | fdn_235, fdn_81 | most cards |\n| Replacement effects (zone redirect) | `register_replacement_effects(self, game)` hook + `ReplacementEffect`; set `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"` | fdn_244, fdn_137 | sos_1 (\"exile instead\") |\n| Loyalty abilities | `Planeswalker` + `get_loyalty_abilities()` → `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; read targets from `self.chosen_targets` (the engine sets it from the activation's targets; mirror fdn_81 only for the loyalty scaffolding, not its `_resolve_target` reads) | fdn_44, fdn_81 | sos_97 |\n| Mana abilities | `Land` + `get_mana_abilities()` → `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` | (grep fdn lands) | sos_257 |\n| Counter target spell | card-local: mirror an FDN counterspell's local `_counter_spell` (pop from stack → graveyard) + `can_cast` guard + `zone=Zone.STACK` targeting | fdn_48 (Refute) | sos_57 |\n| Tokens | `create_token(game, player, token)` in `engine/game.py` | fdn_44, fdn_81 | sos_13 |\n| Reanimate (graveyard → battlefield) | `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB automatically) | — | sos_97 (−2) |\n| Helpers | `engine/game.py`: `draw_card`, `discard`, `deal_damage`, `exile`, `sacrifice`, `add_counter`, `tap`/`untap` | — | many |\n\nBefore adding anything to `engine/`, confirm the seam above doesn't already do\nthe job. The first question for every clause is **\"which FDN card and which\nexisting hook already does this?\"** — not \"what new system do I need?\".\n\n## Build these three shared engine changes FIRST (small, additive)\n\nEach is reused by more than one card. Build and verify them up front so the cards\nthat depend on them just register ordinary triggers/hooks. Keep each tiny; run\n`python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each.\n\n- **E1 — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`.** It is defined in `engine/events.py`\n  (fields: `spell`, `card`, `controller`) but **never fired**. Fire it inside\n  `cast_spell` (`engine/casting.py`) right after the spell is pushed to the stack,\n  populating `spell=<the StackObject>`, `card`, and `controller`. Copies made by\n  `copy_spell` do **not** go through `cast_spell`, so they correctly do not\n  re-fire it. *Reused by:* sos_226 (Casualty), sos_257 (animated pump).\n- **E2 — Add `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`.** No event fires at any\n  main phase today. Add the event class to `engine/events.py` (model it on the\n  fieldless `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`) and fire it from\n  `GameState.advance_phase` (`engine/game_state.py`) — the single chokepoint every\n  phase transition passes through — when the new phase becomes `PRECOMBAT_MAIN`,\n  right **after** `empty_mana_pools()` so anything a handler adds to the pool\n  survives into the main phase. Firing it here (not in `engine/turn.py`) makes it\n  behave identically whether a turn is run normally or the state is advanced\n  directly; a handler fired only from the turn loop would be skipped on a direct\n  advance. Handlers identify \"your main phase\" by checking the active player.\n  (Contrast E1, which belongs in `cast_spell` because casting always flows through\n  that path.) *Reused by:* sos_57 (next main phase, once), sos_120 (each of your\n  first main phases, recurring).\n- **E3 — Aggregate cost reduction from the battlefield.** `get_cost_reduction`\n  (`engine/casting.py`) only calls the spell's own `cost_reduction` hook. Extend\n  it to also add reductions contributed by the caster's battlefield permanents:\n  for each permanent exposing `spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell) -> int`,\n  add it when the spell being cast is an instant/sorcery. Clamp as today\n  (generic-only, ≥ 0). *Reused by:* sos_245 (grants affinity to your spells); any\n  future \"your spells cost less\" card. (sos_1 / sos_245 self-reduction still use\n  the normal `cost_reduction` hook.)\n\n## Per-card gaps — keep them CARD-LOCAL\n\nThe remaining mechanics each serve **exactly one card**. Implement each as the\nsmallest local change in that card's `card_impl.py` (plus the tiny additive\nengine edit noted), and add a one-line comment on any deliberate limitation. Do\n**not** generalize these into engine subsystems. Specifics live in the per-card\nitems below: Miracle (sos_201), the split/back-face (sos_13), the restricted-mana\ntag + land animation (sos_257), and coin-flips / skip-turns / surveil (sos_97).\n\n**E1–E3 and the per-card edits below are not an exhaustive list of the engine\nchanges you may make.** If a card genuinely needs an engine change that isn't\nlisted — a new event, a field on a permanent or on game state, a small helper —\nyou are free to add it. The bar is *minimal, additive, and justified by a real\ncard need*, not a fixed whitelist; what to avoid is a speculative general\n*subsystem* for one card's mechanic, not engine edits as such. Whenever you touch\n`engine/`, keep the change as small as possible, comment any deliberate\nlimitation, never rename/move/delete existing symbols, and keep `engine_tests/`\ngreen.\n\n## Build order\n\nWork the items **in order, one at a time**. Items E1–E3 are the shared engine\nchanges above; the card items follow in dependency order (shared seams first,\nthen the cards that reuse them; simplest → hardest). For every card: read its\n`card_spec.json`, enumerate each oracle clause and its edges, mirror the nearest\nFDN card, reuse the named seam, write 2–5 real-engine tests through `test_utils`,\nthen run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` before moving on.\n\n- [ ] **E1 — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell`** (see above). Verify\n  with a probe trigger that casting an instant fires it once with the right\n  `controller` and `spell`.\n- [ ] **E2 — Add + fire `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`** from\n  `GameState.advance_phase`, after `empty_mana_pools()` (see above). Verify a\n  registered trigger fires — and any mana it adds persists — when the state is\n  advanced directly to the active player's precombat main.\n- [ ] **E3 — Battlefield cost-reduction aggregation in `get_cost_reduction`**\n  (see above). Verify a permanent exposing `spell_cost_reduction` reduces an\n  instant's generic cost, clamped at 0.\n\n- [ ] **sos_4 — Together as One** *(warm-up: mana-spent, pure resolve)*\n  - Clauses: Converge — X = number of colors of mana spent; target player draws\n    X, deal X damage to any target, you gain X life.\n  - Reuse: read `card.colors_spent` in `on_resolve`; `X = len(set(colors_spent))`.\n    `draw_card`, `deal_damage`; set life directly. Targets via\n    `get_targets`/`self.chosen_targets`.\n  - Edges: X = 0 (colorless cast) → draws/deals/gains 0; \"any target\" is a player\n    or creature. Tests set colors deterministically via `mana_pool.pay(choices=)`.\n\n- [ ] **sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic** *(cost reduction + free cast + trigger + replacement)*\n  - Clauses: costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard; Reach; on\n    attack, may cast target instant/sorcery from graveyard for free (if only one\n    legal target, auto-select it instead of prompting); if that spell would go to\n    the graveyard, exile it instead.\n  - Reuse: `cost_reduction` hook (count instant/sorcery in your graveyard);\n    `Keyword` for Reach; `register_triggers` on `AttacksTriggeredEvent`;\n    `cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`; for exile-instead,\n    register a `ReplacementEffect` that sets the spell's\n    `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"`.\n  - Edges: empty graveyard (no reduction; \"may\" trigger with no legal target);\n    reduction is generic-only and clamps at 0.\n\n- [ ] **sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer** *(uses E3; affinity self + grant)*\n  - Clauses: Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control);\n    Flying, Deathtouch; your instant/sorcery spells also have affinity for creatures.\n  - Reuse: `cost_reduction` hook for its OWN affinity (count creatures you\n    control); `Keyword.FLYING | DEATHTOUCH`. For the grant, expose\n    `spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)` returning your creature count — E3\n    aggregates it into other spells' costs. No per-spell edits.\n  - Edges: 0 creatures (no reduction); generic-only.\n\n- [ ] **sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant** *(uses E1; spell copy + casualty)*\n  - Clauses: Flying, Vigilance; your instant/sorcery spells have Casualty 1.\n  - Reuse: `register_triggers` on `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (now fired by E1),\n    gated to instant/sorcery spells you cast while Silverquill is on the\n    battlefield. On trigger, prompt once for the creature to sacrifice (one\n    `choose_card`; the answer is the creature, or `None` to decline — no separate\n    yes/no), and accept it only if its power ≥ 1 (`sacrifice`); if a creature is\n    sacrificed, `copy_spell(game, event.spell, controller)` (the copy goes on the\n    stack above the original and may choose new targets).\n  - Edges: no creature with power ≥ 1 → casualty simply not taken; the copy is\n    not itself \"cast\" (E1 won't re-fire for it — correct).\n\n- [ ] **sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex** *(uses E1; land: mana + restriction + animation)*\n  - Clauses: {T}: add {C}; {T}, pay 1 life: add one mana of any color usable only\n    to cast an instant/sorcery; {5}: if not already a creature, becomes a 2/4\n    Wizard (still a land) with \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery, +1/+0 until EOT\".\n  - Reuse: `Land` + `get_mana_abilities()` for the two mana abilities. The `{5}`\n    animation is an **activated** ability — expose it via\n    `get_activated_abilities(self)` (the engine calls this hook with no arguments\n    and addresses abilities by printed index; do not add parameters to it). Read\n    any state it needs from `self` — gate the animation on\n    `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types` — not from a hook argument.\n    `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (E1) drives the animated pump.\n    **Restricted mana (gap):** add a lightweight restriction marker\n    to mana in the pool and honor it at payment time so that mana can only pay for\n    instant/sorcery spells (small additive change in `engine/mana.py`).\n    **Animation (gap):** mutate in place — add the Creature type, base P/T 2/4, the\n    Wizard subtype, and register the pump trigger; it stays a land. Do not make a\n    new permanent.\n  - Edges: animate only if not already a creature; the land has been on the\n    battlefield, so no summoning sickness concern for the {5} clause; pump stacks\n    per spell and resets end of turn; restricted mana cannot pay for a creature.\n\n- [ ] **sos_57 — Mana Sculpt** *(counter via fdn_48; uses E2)*\n  - Clauses: counter target spell; if you control a Wizard, at the beginning of\n    your next main phase add {C} equal to the mana spent to cast that spell.\n  - Reuse: mirror **fdn_48 (Refute)** for the counter (local `_counter_spell`,\n    `can_cast` guard, `zone=Zone.STACK` target). Record the countered spell's\n    mana **spent** (amount, not mana value). Delayed mana: register a trigger on\n    `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` (E2) stamped with the cast turn;\n    when it next fires for you, if you control a Wizard add that much {C}, then\n    unregister (one-shot).\n  - Edges: no Wizard → no delayed mana; \"mana spent\" is the amount actually paid.\n\n- [ ] **sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone** *(cast-from-exile + copy; uses E2 for Paradigm)*\n  - Clauses: exile from top of library until total mana value ≥ 4; may cast any\n    number of them for free; Paradigm (after it first resolves, exile it; then at\n    the beginning of each of your first main phases, may cast a copy from exile\n    for free).\n  - Reuse: library top access to peel cards (`library.top(n)`; top = last index);\n    `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`; `copy_spell` for the Paradigm copy.\n    Paradigm: on resolve exile the Capstone, then register a recurring trigger on\n    `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` (E2) for your first main phase.\n  - Edges: library runs out before MV 4; non-castable exiled cards (lands) stay\n    exiled; \"first main phase\" = precombat main, recurring.\n\n- [ ] **sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares** *(uses cast-from-exile; token + prepared)*\n  - Clauses: ETB — target player creates a 1/1 white-black Inkling with flying;\n    then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes prepared;\n    while prepared you may cast a copy of its spell (Swords to Plowshares),\n    which unprepares it.\n  - Reuse: one Creature class `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares` (3/3 Cat Cleric).\n    **Bake its identity in so the class constructs bare** — set `name` to the full\n    card name from `card_spec.json`, exactly `\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to\n    Plowshares\"` (a double-faced card's name is the whole `front // back` string,\n    not just the front face). The engine and tests instantiate the card with no\n    arguments and key off `name`, so a front-face-only name makes it unfindable.\n    Add a `SwordsToPlowshares(Instant)` **helper class in the same file** (exile\n    target creature; its controller gains life = its power). `register_triggers`\n    on `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`; `create_token`. When prepared and the\n    player elects: create an **actual copy** of the Swords instant, put it in\n    exile, and **cast it from exile** via `cast_spell_free(..., Zone.EXILE)`, then\n    unprepare. (Per the rulebook the prepared spell is a real Swords copy castable\n    from exile — confirm cost semantics in `RULEBOOK.txt`.)\n  - Edges: opponent does NOT control more creatures → not prepared; Swords on an\n    empty board (no legal target).\n\n- [ ] **sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian** *(miracle card-local via draw event; upkeep loot)*\n  - Clauses: Flying, Haste; instant/sorcery cards in your hand have miracle {2};\n    at the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card to draw one.\n  - Reuse: `Keyword.FLYING | HASTE`; `register_triggers` on\n    `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` gated to an opponent's upkeep; `discard` +\n    `draw_card`. **Miracle (gap, card-local):** register on\n    `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` (already fired by `draw_card`), gated to your\n    **first draw this turn** (track with a turn-stamped flag) AND drawn card is\n    instant/sorcery; then you may cast it for the miracle cost by deducting {2}\n    and using the free-cast stack path. Continuous effects do not reach the hand,\n    so do not try to tag hand cards.\n  - Edges: not the first card drawn this turn → no miracle; loot is optional;\n    empty hand.\n\n- [ ] **sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer** *(planeswalker; surveil / reanimate / coin-flip / skip-turns)*\n  - Clauses: starting loyalty 3; +1 Surveil 2; −1 any number of target players\n    each discard a card; −2 return a creature card with mana value ≤ 3 from your\n    graveyard to the battlefield; −7 flip five coins, target opponent skips their\n    next X turns (X = heads).\n  - Reuse: `Planeswalker` + `get_loyalty_abilities()` (mirror **fdn_81 / fdn_44**\n    for the loyalty-ability scaffolding, but read this card's targets from\n    `self.chosen_targets`, which the engine sets from the activation's `targets`\n    — do not use `_resolve_target` / `_resolve_targets`). −2 reanimate via\n    `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB). +1\n    Surveil 2: look at `library.top(2)`, bin to graveyard or keep on top (small\n    local helper; player choice in tests). **Coin flip (gap):** flip each coin\n    with `random.Random.randint(0, 1)` via a seeded RNG — add a `game.rng`\n    (`random.Random`) if absent so tests are deterministic. **Skip turns\n    (gap):** record the count as a `skip_turns` attribute on the targeted player\n    (`target_player.skip_turns += X`), and have the turn loop\n    (`engine/game_state.py` advance logic) check and decrement it; X heads → skip\n    that player's next X turns.\n  - Edges: −2 with no valid creature in graveyard; −1 with zero target players;\n    ultimate only at loyalty ≥ 7; X = 0 heads skips nothing.\n\n## Pitfalls (read before writing engine code)\n\n1. **A new subsystem for a one-card mechanic is the trap.** It is tempting to\n   build generic miracle/casualty/affinity/paradigm/animation/preparation systems\n   — but each here serves exactly one card, and that path balloons into sprawling,\n   speculative machinery that drifts from the cards' real behavior. E1–E3 are the\n   *shared* engine changes worth building up front (each reused by ≥ 2 cards);\n   beyond them, add small additive engine edits whenever a single card genuinely\n   needs one — just never a general *subsystem* for a one-card mechanic. If you're\n   adding a manager, framework, or registry for something only one card uses, stop\n   and make it card-local instead.\n2. **Your own green tests are not proof.** Tests you write can encode the same\n   misreading as your code — passing them only proves the code matches your\n   reading, not the card. After each card, re-derive the behavior from\n   `card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt` and run a short **throwaway** smoke check\n   through `test_utils` that you did *not* write a test for — assert the\n   spec-observable result (zones, life, P/T, counters, exile vs graveyard).\n3. **Test through the real engine, never a stand-in.** Drive behavior via\n   `test_utils` (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, `cast_spell`, `advance_to_phase`,\n   `declare_attackers`, `declare_blockers`; for abilities, `ActivateAbility(card, index)`\n   resolved through `priority_loop` and scripted with `DeterministicPlayer`).\n   Abilities are addressed by printed index, the same way the engine activates them.\n   Do not hand-build internal events, call a card's `get_*_abilities()` or\n   `on_resolve` directly, pop the stack, or script a player's internal queue —\n   those pass while the real path is broken.\n4. **Reuse before you add.** For every clause, name the FDN card and existing hook\n   that already does it before writing anything new. The seam table is the\n   starting point; the FDN library is the rest.\n5. **Additive-only, and keep `engine_tests/` green.** Add/extend in `engine/`; never\n   rename/move/delete existing symbols — other modules import them by name, so a\n   rename or move breaks those imports. Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q`\n   after every card and every engine change; never ship a regression.\n6. **Stay in the assigned file.** Each card's class lives in its own\n   `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`; do not move or rename card directories. Do not\n   edit `engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/*/tests.py`.\n","numLines":300,"startLine":1,"totalLines":300}}}
