{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PTTnfe6wDcYaX6ArXuHvQS","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25473cdc-0503-4b45-9076-b9d3fca79f4a","uuid":"4c99966d-5e69-4deb-98ca-66b476f6fdfd","timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:23:29.692Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- **No-legal-target guard:** the engine's `cast_spell_free` accepts a `None`\n  target without rejecting, so `cast_prepared_spell` guards on the presence of a\n  creature; with none it returns False and stays prepared.","newString":"- **No-legal-target guard:** the engine's `cast_spell_free` accepts a `None`\n  target without rejecting, so `cast_prepared_spell` guards on the presence of a\n  creature; with none it returns False and stays prepared.\n\n## sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n- **Coin flips (gap, additive):** added `game.rng = random.Random()` to\n  `GameState.__init__`. The ultimate flips via `game.rng.randint(0, 1)`; tests\n  reseed `game.rng` for determinism.\n- **Skip turns (gap, additive):** added `Player.skip_turns` and handling in\n  `advance_phase`'s turn-wrap — if the normally-next player is skipping, consume\n  one skip and pass the turn to the other player (the skipping player stays\n  \"due\" until their skips are exhausted). No-skip behavior is identical to\n  before (guarded on `skip_turns > 0`), so existing rotation tests pass.\n- **Loyalty-ability targets:** the engine's loyalty activation path doesn't\n  thread targets onto the planeswalker, so effects read `self.chosen_targets`,\n  which tests set directly before activating (per the build plan).","originalFile":"# KEY_DECISIONS.md\n\nLightweight log of ambiguous-clause decisions, deviations from TODO.md, and\ndeliberate card-local engine limitations made during the SOS card build.\n\n## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic\n- **Engine gap (additive):** `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined in events.py but\n  never fired anywhere. Added per-attacker firing in `declare_attackers_step`\n  (engine/combat.py). No-op when no trigger is registered, so existing tests\n  unaffected; this also makes FDN attack-trigger cards (Etali, Drakuseth) live.\n- **Exile-instead clause:** TODO suggested a `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`\n  redirect, but the engine only consults replacement effects for permanents\n  *leaving the battlefield*, not for a spell resolving stack→graveyard. Per the\n  pitfalls' explicit preference (\"a flag/field read at the one right point\"), I\n  added a card-local `_resolve_to_zone` attribute read in `_resolve_spell`\n  (default graveyard, consumed after use). The Dawning Archaic sets it to\n  `Zone.EXILE` on the spell it casts for free.\n- **\"may\" with single target:** per TODO, when exactly one legal instant/sorcery\n  is in the graveyard it is auto-selected (no prompt); with multiple, the player\n  picks via `choose_card` (or `None` to decline).\n\n## sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n- **Restricted mana (gap, additive):** added a per-type `_restricted` count to\n  `ManaPool`, an `add(..., restricted=True)` flag, and an `allow_restricted`\n  kwarg on `can_pay`/`pay` (default `True` → all existing behavior unchanged).\n  `cast_spell` passes `allow_restricted = card is instant/sorcery`. Models the\n  single restriction this card needs (\"instant/sorcery only\"); not a general\n  restriction subsystem.\n- **`AttacksTriggeredEvent` reuse:** the pump and combat rely on the\n  declare-attackers firing added for sos_1.\n- **Animation (gap, card-local):** the card subclasses `Land` (NOT `Creature`,\n  to avoid combat's `hasattr(base_power)` treating an un-animated land as an\n  attacker). `power`/`toughness` are properties that raise `AttributeError`\n  until animated, so combat/SBA `hasattr` checks skip the un-animated land.\n  `_animate` mutates in place: adds the CREATURE type (and updates\n  `_original_card_types` so it persists through effect resets), the Wizard\n  subtype, base 2/4, the creature runtime attrs, and registers the pump trigger.\n- **Pump \"+1/+0 until EOT\":** `apply_all` only runs at cleanup, so the pump\n  bumps `modified_power` directly (immediately visible) and the cleanup\n  effect-manager reset (`_reset_characteristics`) clears it — exactly the\n  until-end-of-turn duration.\n\n## sos_57 — Mana Sculpt\n- **`mana_spent` (gap, additive):** the engine tracked `colors_spent` but not the\n  *amount* of mana spent. Added `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` in\n  `cast_spell` (and `= 0` in `cast_spell_free`). The spec says \"amount of mana\n  spent\" (not mana value), so this correctly reflects cost reductions.\n- **Wizard timing (ambiguous → followed plan):** \"If you control a Wizard, add …\n  at the beginning of your next main phase.\" Checked the Wizard condition at the\n  delayed firing (per TODO), not at resolution.\n- **\"next main phase\" limitation:** modeled as your next *precombat* main via the\n  E2 event (postcombat main is not a fire point). The delayed trigger is a\n  one-shot stamped with the cast turn (fires when `active_player is you and\n  turn_number > setup_turn`).\n\n## sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n- **ETB in `on_resolve`, not a self-ETB trigger (engine vs plan):** TODO said\n  `register_triggers` on `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, but `move_to_zone`\n  fires a permanent's enter event *before* registering its own triggers, so a\n  self-watching ETB trigger never fires on its own entry (verified empirically).\n  Implemented the ETB in `on_resolve` like FDN ETB creatures. To get the right\n  \"opponent controls more creatures than you\" count, Emeritus is counted among\n  your creatures (+1) since it's resolving and about to enter.\n- **Prepared copy cost (ambiguous → followed plan):** \"you may cast a copy of its\n  spell\" — cost not specified by CONTEXT.md / no exact rulebook entry for the\n  SOS-specific \"prepared\". Per TODO, cast the Swords copy from exile for free via\n  `cast_spell_free`; it ends in the graveyard after resolving. Casting unprepares.\n- **No-legal-target guard:** the engine's `cast_spell_free` accepts a `None`\n  target without rejecting, so `cast_prepared_spell` guards on the presence of a\n  creature; with none it returns False and stays prepared.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":69,"oldLines":3,"newStart":69,"newLines":16,"lines":["   target without rejecting, so `cast_prepared_spell` guards on the presence of a","   creature; with none it returns False and stays prepared."," ","+## sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer","+- **Coin flips (gap, additive):** added `game.rng = random.Random()` to","+  `GameState.__init__`. The ultimate flips via `game.rng.randint(0, 1)`; tests","+  reseed `game.rng` for determinism.","+- **Skip turns (gap, additive):** added `Player.skip_turns` and handling in","+  `advance_phase`'s turn-wrap — if the normally-next player is skipping, consume","+  one skip and pass the turn to the other player (the skipping player stays","+  \"due\" until their skips are exhausted). No-skip behavior is identical to","+  before (guarded on `skip_turns > 0`), so existing rotation tests pass.","+- **Loyalty-ability targets:** the engine's loyalty activation path doesn't","+  thread targets onto the planeswalker, so effects read `self.chosen_targets`,","+  which tests set directly before activating (per the build plan).","+"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
