{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01WeL6q7aQWxxoPiWvy6beoY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. Here's a summary of the completed run.\n\n## SOS card implementation — complete\n\nAll **13 checklist items** are implemented, tested through the real engine, verified independently against the spec, and committed (one commit per card). Final state:\n- **`engine_tests/`: 1145 passed** (zero regressions across every engine change)\n- **Full suite: 1268 passed** (engine + FDN reference tests + all 10 SOS card tests)\n- All ten card classes import cleanly and construct bare with correct names.\n\n### Shared engine seams built first (E1–E3)\n- **E1** — fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell` (was defined, never fired). Drives Casualty + the animated-land pump.\n- **E2** — add + fire `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` from `advance_phase` (after `empty_mana_pools`). Drives Mana Sculpt's delayed mana and Paradigm.\n- **E3** — aggregate battlefield `spell_cost_reduction` for instant/sorcery casts in `get_cost_reduction`. Drives Witherbloom's granted affinity.\n\n### The ten cards\nsos_4 (Converge), sos_1 (cost-reduction + free-cast attack trigger + exile-instead), sos_245 (affinity self + grant), sos_226 (Casualty + copy), sos_257 (land: restricted mana + animation + pump), sos_57 (counter + delayed mana), sos_120 (cast-from-exile + Paradigm recurring copy), sos_13 (DFC token + prepared), sos_201 (miracle + upkeep loot), sos_97 (planeswalker: surveil/reanimate/coin-flip/skip-turns).\n\n### Engine gaps — kept minimal & additive (logged in `KEY_DECISIONS.md`)\nEach was a small flag/field or a single additive edit at the one right point — never a subsystem: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` firing, a `_resolve_to_zone` exile-redirect flag, instant/sorcery-restricted mana on `ManaPool`, `card.mana_spent` tracking, `game.rng`, and `Player.skip_turns` + turn-wrap handling.\n\n### Notable spec-over-plan corrections\n- **sos_13**: the engine fires a permanent's enter event *before* registering its own triggers (verified empirically), so a self-ETB trigger never fires — implemented the ETB in `on_resolve` like the FDN ETB creatures, counting Emeritus itself among \"your\" creatures.\n- **sos_201**: `cards_drawn_this_turn` is never reset, so \"first draw this turn\" uses a turn-stamped marker instead.\n- **sos_257**: subclassed `Land` (not `Creature`) with `power`/`toughness` that raise `AttributeError` until animated, so `hasattr` checks in combat/SBAs correctly skip the un-animated land."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":413010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":423},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25473cdc-0503-4b45-9076-b9d3fca79f4a","uuid":"9b220c67-7419-40a1-bc9c-73cdc0f560ea","request_id":"req_011Cbuy6gi3KhBpHzhQRLJe8"}
